.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/engine.io-parser Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "engine\&.io-parser"
.PP
\fR\fP \fR\fP

.PP
This is the JavaScript parser for the engine\&.io protocol encoding, shared by both \fRengine\&.io-client\fP and \fRengine\&.io\fP\&.
.SH "How to use"
.PP
.SS "Standalone"
The parser can encode/decode packets, payloads, and payloads as binary with the following methods: \fRencodePacket\fP, \fRdecodePacket\fP, \fRencodePayload\fP, \fRdecodePayload\fP\&.

.PP
Example:

.PP
.PP
.nf
const parser = require("engine\&.io\-parser");
const data = Buffer\&.from([ 1, 2, 3, 4 ]);

parser\&.encodePacket({ type: "message", data }, encoded => {
  const decodedData = parser\&.decodePacket(encoded); // decodedData === data
});
.fi
.PP
.SS "With browserify"
Engine\&.IO Parser is a commonjs module, which means you can include it by using \fRrequire\fP on the browser and package using \fRbrowserify\fP:

.PP
.IP "1." 4
install the parser package

.PP
.PP
.nf
npm install engine\&.io\-parser
.fi
.PP

.PP
.IP "1." 4
write your app code

.PP
.PP
.nf
const parser = require("engine\&.io\-parser");

const testBuffer = new Int8Array(10);
for (let i = 0; i < testBuffer\&.length; i++) testBuffer[i] = i;

const packets = [{ type: "message", data: testBuffer\&.buffer }, { type: "message", data: "hello" }];

parser\&.encodePayload(packets, encoded => {
  parser\&.decodePayload(encoded,
    (packet, index, total) => {
      const isLast = index + 1 == total;
      if (!isLast) {
        const buffer = new Int8Array(packet\&.data); // testBuffer
      } else {
        const message = packet\&.data; // "hello"
      }
    });
});
.fi
.PP

.PP
.IP "1." 4
build your app bundle

.PP
.PP
.nf
$ browserify app\&.js > bundle\&.js
.fi
.PP

.PP
.IP "1." 4
include on your page

.PP
.PP
.nf
<script src="/path/to/bundle\&.js"></script>
.fi
.PP

.PP
.SH "Features"
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Runs on browser and node\&.js seamlessly
.IP "\(bu" 2
Runs inside HTML5 WebWorker
.IP "\(bu" 2
Can encode and decode packets
.IP "  \(bu" 4
Encodes from/to ArrayBuffer or Blob when in browser, and Buffer or ArrayBuffer in Node
.PP

.PP
.SH "API"
.PP
Note: \fRcb(type)\fP means the type is a callback function that contains a parameter of type \fRtype\fP when called\&.
.SS "Node"
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRencodePacket\fP
.IP "  \(bu" 4
Encodes a packet\&.
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fBParameters\fP
.IP "    \(bu" 6
\fRObject\fP: the packet to encode, has \fRtype\fP and \fRdata\fP\&.
.IP "      \(bu" 8
\fRdata\fP: can be a \fRString\fP, \fRNumber\fP, \fRBuffer\fP, \fRArrayBuffer\fP
.PP

.IP "    \(bu" 6
\fRBoolean\fP: binary support
.IP "    \(bu" 6
\fRFunction\fP: callback, returns the encoded packet (\fRcb(String)\fP)
.PP

.PP

.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRdecodePacket\fP
.IP "  \(bu" 4
Decodes a packet\&. Data also available as an ArrayBuffer if requested\&.
.IP "  \(bu" 4
Returns data as \fRString\fP or (\fRBlob\fP on browser, \fRArrayBuffer\fP on Node)
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fBParameters\fP
.IP "    \(bu" 6
\fRString\fP | \fRArrayBuffer\fP: the packet to decode, has \fRtype\fP and \fRdata\fP
.IP "    \(bu" 6
\fRString\fP: optional, the binary type
.PP

.PP

.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRencodePayload\fP
.IP "  \(bu" 4
Encodes multiple messages (payload)\&.
.IP "  \(bu" 4
If any contents are binary, they will be encoded as base64 strings\&. Base64 encoded strings are marked with a b before the length specifier
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fBParameters\fP
.IP "    \(bu" 6
\fRArray\fP: an array of packets
.IP "    \(bu" 6
\fRFunction\fP: callback, returns the encoded payload (\fRcb(String)\fP)
.PP

.PP

.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRdecodePayload\fP
.IP "  \(bu" 4
Decodes data when a payload is maybe expected\&. Possible binary contents are decoded from their base64 representation\&.
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fBParameters\fP
.IP "    \(bu" 6
\fRString\fP: the payload
.IP "    \(bu" 6
\fRFunction\fP: callback, returns (cb(\fRObject\fP: packet, \fRNumber\fP:packet index, \fRNumber\fP:packet total))
.PP

.PP

.PP
.SH "Tests"
.PP
Standalone tests can be run with \fRnpm test\fP which will run the node\&.js tests\&.

.PP
Browser tests are run using \fRzuul\fP\&. (You must have zuul setup with a saucelabs account\&.)

.PP
You can run the tests locally using the following command:

.PP
.PP
.nf
npm run test:browser
.fi
.PP
